          { name: "Running on Cultural Issues Rather Than Economic Grievance", tag: "avoid", why: "AL-HD-8 at $60,934 median income, 38.4% renter rate, and 40% people of color is not a district where cultural conservatism is the primary organizing principle — it is a district where whether a household can afford rent and pay for healthcare is the daily reality. Any candidate who leads with cultural positioning rather than economic security cedes the most material conversation to the opposition. In a working-class, plurality-minority district, the candidate who speaks credibly about jobs and wages wins; the candidate who prioritizes cultural battles loses the economic narrative." }
