          { name: "Neglecting to Build Specific Constituent Relationships Across the 27% Hispanic Population", tag: "avoid", why: "A district where more than one in four residents is Hispanic cannot be represented effectively through generic outreach or by assuming Hispanic voters will remain aligned with one party regardless of specific legislative record or constituent attention. The 2022 result provides no evidence of Hispanic voter preference — only that the overall district went 88-12. If that margin was driven by concentrated Anglo support or by an exceptionally weak opposition candidate rather than by genuine Hispanic voter allegiance, a credible challenger with authentic Hispanic community relationships will find a substantially more competitive seat than the 88-12 headline suggests. Building genuine, ongoing relationships with Hispanic civic, business, and community leaders; attending community events; and delivering specific constituent service across the 27% of the district you represent is not optional for a durable incumbent." }
