          { name: "Pursuing Partisan Conflict Over Local Governance Pragmatism", tag: "avoid", why: "In a district this homogeneous and this strongly Republican, the incumbent's political sustainability depends on being seen as pragmatic and focused on local results rather than as an ideological combatant in state or national partisan wars. A working-class homeowner at $60,879 income who voted for Gidley with 94% support is likely evaluating based on local governance competence and perceived alignment with property-owner interests, not on ideological purity or partisan conflict intensity. A representative who becomes known primarily for state-level partisan positioning rather than for delivering local results risks disappointing a constituency that chose them based on expectations of practical governance." }
