          "Lead on housing affordability and cost of living: the 41.9% renter rate and $79,434 income signal a constituency managing real housing and affordability pressure in what is likely an appreciating real estate market; a legislative agenda that addresses zoning, rental protections, property tax fairness, and the relationship between education funding and opportunity for young families is more credible than abstract conservative positioning.",
          "Engage the college-educated constituency on fiscal competence and education quality: at 49.6% college attainment, this district has voters with direct stakes in K-12 and higher education funding, teacher compensation, and the workforce pipeline; Shaw must articulate a specific vision for education quality and funding sustainability rather than generic rhetoric about government efficiency.",
          "Do not treat the 64% margin as insulating against demographic change: the 23.71% Black population, 11.41% Hispanic and Asian combined, and high renter rate all represent constituencies with material concerns that are activated by credible opposition candidates; the margin is healthy now, but it is earned through active constituent engagement, not guaranteed by partisan alignment in a college-educated, economically mobile district."
