          { name: "Healthcare Affordability & Rural Service Access", tag: "lean-into", why: "In a district with a 37.8-year median age and $60,223 income, healthcare costs are a direct household budget pressure for working-class families navigating the gap between modest incomes and rising medical expenses. Rural service delivery — hospital viability, primary care access, prescription drug costs — are practical governance concerns that affect daily quality of life. A legislative agenda that engages healthcare affordability with specificity, rather than deferring to abstract market positioning, demonstrates that representation is about constituent needs rather than party orthodoxy." },
          { name: "The Unexplained 10% Opposition", tag: "careful", why: "A 90-10 result in a deeply red state could represent either overwhelming consolidation or masking of genuine local frustration that a more engaged challenger could mobilize. The opposition could reflect working-class economic anxiety, a specific incumbent failure, or simply the baseline Democratic turnout in any election. Without understanding what the 10% actually represents — through actual constituent engagement, not assumption — a representative risks being surprised by erosion if opposition energy increases or if a credible alternative emerges who addresses unmet concerns." },
          { name: "Treating 90% as a Permanent Floor Rather Than an Earned Margin", tag: "avoid", why: "A 90-10 result is not a mandate for inattention; it is a result that must be re-earned in the next cycle. In a working-class district where economic concerns are material rather than abstract, a representative who campaigns as though the margin is guaranteed — rather than treating it as a high baseline that requires continuous constituent engagement on concrete issues — invites erosion from a challenger who takes those material concerns seriously. The 10% opposition is a signal to listen, not a signal to ignore." },
          { name: "Confusing Party Loyalty with Constituent Service", tag: "avoid", why: "AL-HD-64's Republican advantage reflects the district's demographic and cultural alignment with the Republican Party, not unconditional support for any candidate or any legislative agenda regardless of outcomes. A representative who behaves as though working-class Republican voters will remain loyal regardless of whether their economic concerns are addressed misunderstands the constituency. Working-class voters in both parties evaluate on whether government is delivering for them — and a representative who treats the 90% as permission to ignore constituent feedback on economic security will find that margin eroding faster than expected." }
