          "Address younger adults' economic mobility directly: at 33.8 median age with 40% Democratic opposition, the district's young people are evaluating on whether they can build economic security in southwestern Oklahoma or need to leave—housing costs, healthcare access, and agricultural or tribal enterprise employment pathways are the material concerns that determine whether this cohort stays engaged with the incumbent.",
          "Engage the agricultural economy with specificity: water rights, irrigation infrastructure, cotton and wheat viability in semi-arid conditions, and rural service delivery are the practical governance issues for farming and ranching families—and these intersect with tribal water rights frameworks in ways that require legislative fluency on both dimensions simultaneously.",
