          "Lead on economic security for working-class households at $46,799 income: wage standards, job quality, childcare affordability, and protection against exploitative rental practices are the material concerns that drive satisfaction or frustration in a district this demographically cohesive.",
          "Invest in turnout reliability and voter contact in Democratic primary cycles; without Republican opposition, the competitive pressure comes from potential primary challenges or declining propensity among lower-engagement voters—both addressed by treating this seat as requiring active electoral work, not passive incumbency.",
          "Engage the 40.3% non-Black constituency (35.23% white, plus smaller Hispanic and Asian populations) with specific constituent attention rather than assuming they are either hostile or irrelevant; in a supermajority-Black district, minority communities can become invisible, and addressing their material concerns around economic mobility and public service access is both governance obligation and turnout reinforcement."
