          { name: "Treating the White & Hispanic Communities as Negligible", tag: "avoid", why: "With 36.94% white residents and 6.53% Hispanic residents, AL-HD-84 is a plurality-Black district, not a monolithic one — nearly 44% of the population is non-Black. While the Black majority sets the district's primary electoral character, neglecting the material concerns of white and Hispanic communities (both of whom face similar income and educational constraints) means governing less than half the district and creating openings for opposition candidates who credibly engage those communities on economic anxiety, workforce development, or immigration policy. A representative who frames the district only through a Black-community lens, rather than as a working-class district where race intersects with shared economic constraints, misses the actual composition of the constituency." }
