          "The constituency in AL-HD-84 is diverse in racial composition but unified by economic circumstance: nearly three in ten households are renters at $47K median income, which creates vulnerability to housing cost inflation and eviction risk; the 12.9% college-educated population signals limited pathways to skilled employment; and the 38.9-year median age indicates a constituency where many adults are in mid-career with limited advancement prospects. The political implication is that this district will not be held or won through inherited partisan loyalty or appeals to abstract conservative or progressive positioning — it will be held or lost based on whether the representative is delivering concrete results on the material concerns that determine whether families can pay rent, afford healthcare, and see a viable path forward for their children. Any candidate in AL-HD-84 who leads with ideology rather than economic grievance and specific legislative remedies is ceding the district to an opponent who does the reverse. The unopposed status in 2022 may reflect strong constituent satisfaction with Forte, or it may reflect weak opposition recruitment; the only way to know is to test the field against a credible challenger who mobilizes around economic concerns."
