          "Engage the Black community (19.52%) with specific constituent attention and legislative delivery rather than inherited partisan loyalty: workforce development, small business access to credit, healthcare equity, and criminal justice reform are the economic and social concerns that drive Black voter behavior. A credible challenger who focuses on these issues while the incumbent assumes Black support based on party alignment will find this constituency responsive.",
          "Address renter constituency directly: at 31.1%, renters represent nearly one in three households and lack the homeownership anchor that traditionally drives Republican loyalty. Eviction prevention, rent assistance, habitability standards, and affordable housing development are the material concerns of a renter-majority constituency segment; legislative leadership on these issues differentiates a responsive incumbent from a party-position legislator.",
