          "Lead with working-family economic security: housing affordability, utility cost burden, childcare access, and wage growth in accessible careers are the material concerns of a 43.2-year-old median age constituency at below-state-average income. These are not abstract policy areas — they determine whether renters can afford rent and whether fixed-income households can pay utilities. Specific programs, not rhetoric, demonstrate that the incumbent understands these pressures.",
          "Engage the 31.86% Black constituency with institutional specificity: historically Black colleges and universities, minority-owned small business support, workforce development in high-wage trades, and equitable access to healthcare are the concrete governance issues that activate authentic representation in a majority-Black or near-majority-Black district. Generic Democratic messaging about shared values does not substitute for knowing and addressing the specific economic mobility barriers that Black families in this district face.",
