          "Engage the white 39% minority directly on economic issues rather than assuming they are locked into opposition; economic anxiety and job opportunity concerns transcend racial lines in a low-income district, and a candidate who addresses these material concerns credibly can shift margins in either direction.",
          "Treat the unopposed 2022 result as a strategic warning, not a floor: an incumbent who has not faced a contested election may be underestimating either the economic frustration in the district or the potential for a credible challenger to mobilize voters around material concerns that are not being met.",
          "Focus on K-12 education quality and workforce development as a pathway to economic mobility; with 18.1% college attainment and a working-class majority, public schools and job training programs are the most direct levers for improving the district's long-term economic trajectory."
