          "Engage the renter majority with specificity: at 33.2%, renters represent nearly one-third of the district and face a distinct set of economic pressures around housing costs, tenant protections, and residential stability. A constituency this economically precarious is evaluating on whether government is delivering material improvements to their circumstances; framing matters less than evidence of concrete action on the issues renters actually face.",
          "Address the college attainment and economic mobility gap: at 26.2%, college attainment in this district is significantly below state averages, suggesting limited access to the education and training pathways that create economic opportunity. Public education funding, community college affordability, and workforce training programs connected to actual job availability are the direct policy levers for this constituency's long-term economic security.",
          "Prepare for competitive challenges by consolidating the current coalition now: an unopposed victory masks the district's underlying vulnerabilities — and any challenger with specific answers to working-family economic concerns will find an opening. Use this cycle to build a substantive legislative record on the material issues that define this constituency, not merely to maintain demographic advantage. The 59.7% Black majority does not eliminate the risk of a credible challenger if constituents believe the incumbent is not delivering on their economic security."
