          { name: "Treating an Unopposed 2022 Result as Evidence of Electoral Safety", tag: "avoid", why: "The 100% Republican result in 2022 was a reflection of absent Democratic opposition, not overwhelming Republican strength in a district whose demographics (young, educated, renter-heavy, diverse) typically produce competitive races. Any incumbent or observer who treats an unopposed race as evidence of a safe seat is misreading the electoral fundamentals. The demographic profile of AL-HD-101 — particularly the 42% college education, 43% renter rate, and 32.7-year median age — suggests a constituency responsive to material economic concerns and candidate competence, not inherited partisan loyalty." },
          { name: "Defaulting to Partisan Messaging Over Constituent Solutions", tag: "avoid", why: "A young, educated, diverse, renter-heavy constituency evaluates on results and competence, not abstract partisan positioning. An incumbent or candidate who leads with partisan messaging instead of specific solutions to housing costs, education funding, healthcare access, and economic opportunity is conceding the trust-and-competence dimension to any challenger who can speak with specificity to these concerns. In a district this young and educated, voters have high expectations for legislative problem-solving; messaging disconnected from material constituent solutions will be read as evasion, not leadership." }
