          "Lead with working-class economic specificity: at $60,605 income with 14.2% college attainment, the district's households are vulnerable to healthcare cost inflation, housing unaffordability, and wage stagnation. Legislation addressing prescription drug costs, rural healthcare access, workforce development, and housing affordability are the material concerns that retain loyalty — not abstract messaging.",
          "Engage the ~6.6% demographic gap as constituent reality, not demographic artifact: the gap most likely represents Native American residents whose governance expectations around tribal partnership, economic development, and healthcare access require active legislative relationship-building, not passive acknowledgment. Authentic engagement with any tribal nations present in or serving the district prevents this constituency from organizing around an alternative.",
          "Recognize that 20.3% renters represent a sub-constituency with distinct economic concerns: rental affordability, tenant protections, and housing-development policy are issues for renters that homeowners may not prioritize. Specific attention to renter household economic security prevents this segment from organizing separately around a challenger who addresses their concerns more directly."
