          "Build ongoing dialogue with renters and lower-income households on housing policy, eviction prevention, and cost-of-living pressures; unopposed electoral results can obscure real constituent frustration if the representative assumes support without demonstrating responsiveness to the material concerns that dominate working-class household budgeting.",
          "Avoid messaging that frames this district's needs as a special interest or minority constituency concern; the 61.44% Black population and working-class economic profile are not sideline issues in Alabama politics—they are the core of a solidly Democratic base that requires active legislative delivery on economic policy, not symbolic representation."
