          { name: "Abstract Cultural Positioning Over Household Economic Concerns", tag: "avoid", why: "A working-class constituency facing real cost-of-living pressure — healthcare, housing, property taxes, utilities — will not be moved by abstract cultural rhetoric if it does not address their material concerns; any representative who substitutes ideology for specific legislative action on household economic security is failing to represent this district's primary voter concern. In an 87-13 district, the temptation to consolidate the base through cultural messaging is strong, but it is also the pathway to erosion if a challenger offers credible solutions to the material economic concerns that the incumbent has treated as secondary." }
