          "Develop specific economic messaging for the 27.8% renter constituency: housing affordability, wage floor, childcare costs, and job accessibility are the material concerns of younger and lower-income adults for whom homeowner-dominant policy agendas may not register as responsive to their needs.",
          "Lead on working-class homeowner economic security: property tax fairness, infrastructure investment in neighborhood stability, and job quality are the core concerns of the 72.2% homeowner majority at $61,342 income who form the district's electoral foundation.",
          "Do not rely on unopposed incumbency as proof of seat security; an absence of opposition is not the same as absence of latent opposition or constituency concern — any credible challenger who speaks to renter economic concerns or AIAN governance expectations could shift the competitive baseline."
