          { name: "Assuming Inherited Partisan Loyalty Among Younger Adults", tag: "avoid", why: "At 33.6 median age, AL-SD-27 has a younger-than-average Alabama constituency for whom partisan identity is less fixed than for older cohorts and economic concerns drive electoral decisions more directly. A representative who assumes younger adults will vote Republican out of habit—rather than because they perceive the incumbent as delivering on housing, jobs, healthcare, and cost-of-living issues—is strategically exposed if a credible challenger emerges with concrete economic messaging." }
